WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:22.266
Hello! Who are you?

2
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:25.438
I'm a sea otter.

3
00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:30.241
Sea otters are a type of weasel.

4
00:00:30.242 --> 00:00:33.119
Where do you live?

5
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.919
Sea otters live in the Pacific Ocean.

6
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.624
We live in North America and Asia.

7
00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:47.452
Do you ever go on land?

8
00:00:47.453 --> 00:00:51.795
Sea otters go on land to rest sometimes.

9
00:00:51.796 --> 00:00:57.678
But we mostly stay in the water.

10
00:00:57.679 --> 00:01:07.615
We even sleep in the water.

11
00:01:07.616 --> 00:01:13.108
How do you do that?

12
00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:17.107
We float on our backs.

13
00:01:17.108 --> 00:01:21.604
Sometimes we sleep wrapped in kelp.

14
00:01:21.605 --> 00:01:25.997
The kelp keeps us from drifting away.

15
00:01:25.998 --> 00:01:29.141
What do you eat?

16
00:01:29.142 --> 00:01:33.646
Sea otters eat fish and octopuses.

17
00:01:33.647 --> 00:01:38.219
We also like crabs and clams.

18
00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:43.225
We use rocks to break them open.

19
00:01:43.226 --> 00:01:49.644
Your fur looks thick!

20
00:01:49.645 --> 00:01:53.779
Our fur is very thick.

21
00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.782
It's also waterproof.

22
00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:02.982
Our fur keeps us warm and dry.

23
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:07.457
Do you have any enemies?

24
00:02:07.458 --> 00:02:14.383
Killer whales and sharks sometimes eat us.

25
00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:20.783
Our webbed feet help us swim away fast.

26
00:02:20.784 --> 00:02:24.491
I'll see you later.

27
00:02:24.492 --> 00:02:29.178
I need to clean my fur now.

28
00:02:29.179 --> 00:02:37.146
Good-bye, Sea Otter!
